cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NDOS: a framework for organising wet-lab and animal neuroscience data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alikarami
    given-names: Elnaz
repository-code: "https://github.com/Elnazkarami/N-DOS"
# The concept DOI, which always resolves to the newest release. A
# version-specific DOI cannot be named here before that version exists, so
# this stays correct between releases rather than pointing at the wrong one.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23167365"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23167365"
    description: "All versions of NDOS"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23167366"
    description: "Version 0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  A toolkit for recovering, describing and querying pre-publication wet-lab and
  animal neuroscience data that was not organised to any standard. NDOS
  inventories storage without modifying it, reads inside archives without
  extracting them, proposes a structure while labelling every inference as an
  inference, captures metadata through the spreadsheets labs already use,
  answers cohort queries with the evidence behind every match and an explicit
  cannot-be-ruled-out result, records provenance from a figure back to raw
  data, and hands off to BIDS and NWB workflows. It includes a directory
  specification a project can be checked against, which is one component rather
  than the whole system.
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - electrophysiology
  - research data management
  - provenance
  - BIDS
  - NWB
license: Apache-2.0
